title: 'Migrate `pallet-beefy` from the deprecated `ValidateUnsigned` trait to `#[pallet::authorize]`'

doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `pallet-beefy` no longer uses the deprecated `ValidateUnsigned` trait and the
    `#[pallet::validate_unsigned]` attribute. The validation of the three equivocation reporting
    calls moved to `#[pallet::authorize]` callbacks.

    The validation semantics do not change. The callbacks accept only `TransactionSource::Local` and
    `TransactionSource::InBlock`, they check the evidence, and they build the same transaction
    validity as before.

    Two changes affect a runtime that includes this pallet. The `EquivocationReportSystem` bound
    changed from `CreateBare<Call<T>>` to `CreateAuthorizedTransaction<Call<T>>`, and the runtime
    must put `frame_system::AuthorizeCall` in its transaction extension pipeline. The three calls
    now need an authorized origin.

crates:
- name: pallet-beefy
  bump: major
- name: sp-consensus-beefy
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-staking-async-rc-runtime
  bump: major
